{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1795273676,"nonce":"WcZ7SZkWK9JZJZsbMuF5mGb6X44=","message":"Immix against the pool over every benchmark row. x86 NUC, idle machine, HEAD 69978bbd, default builds, 3 interleaved runs per row, medians. Wall time includes start-up.\n\nResult. The geometric mean of immix/pool over 43 rows is 1.000. The 17 Lua rows are in the benchmark folder of zyntax_lua and the 26 Python rows are the bench_*.py files. No row failed and every output matched the pool's. Peak memory is equal on small rows. It is lower on the rows with a large live set: Lua pipeline 142 against 152 MB, Python pipeline 83 against 91 MB and Python tokenize 61 against 66 MB.\n\nSlower than the pool by more than 10%, with the rows' own run time:\n\n| row | pool s | immix s | ratio |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| py any_field | 0.027 | 0.041 | 1.54 |\n| lua mandelbrot_strip | 0.018 | 0.021 | 1.16 |\n| lua binary_trees | 0.150 | 0.172 | 1.15 |\n| py closure_call | 0.021 | 0.024 | 1.14 |\n| py any_cast | 0.015 | 0.017 | 1.12 |\n| lua method_call | 0.036 | 0.040 | 1.11 |\n| py free_function_call_untyped | 0.039 | 0.043 | 1.11 |\n| py inlined_call | 0.040 | 0.045 | 1.11 |\n\nEvery row except binary_trees runs for under 0.05 s, so a few milliseconds move the ratio. Faster than the pool by more than 10%: Lua inlined_call 0.82, Lua free_function_call 0.83, Lua fib 0.91, Python lambda_call 0.70, dict_records 0.90, op_overload 0.90, dict_large 0.91, dict_iter 0.92.\n\nThe one real outlier is py any_field. It allocates and frees a small object a million times. The pool reuses each freed block at once and peaks at 25 MB with 1.5K page faults. Immix ignores an explicit free, so it allocates 32 MB of fresh pages before its first collection. It peaks at 60 MB with 10.4K faults. Lowering the first collection floor recovers most of it:\n\n| floor | wall s | peak MB | faults |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 32 MB (default) | 0.03 to 0.04 | 60 | 10.4K |\n| 16 MB | 0.02 to 0.03 | 43 | 6.0K |\n| 8 MB | 0.02 | 34 | 3.8K |\n| 4 MB | 0.02 | 29 | 2.6K |\n| pool | 0.01 to 0.02 | 25 | 1.5K |\n\nA fixed small floor is not safe. An empty collection costs about 0.3 ms, so a 4 MB floor on a program like w_phase means about 1500 collections. An earlier test also showed a smaller floor slows Lua binary_trees. Two ways to fix any_field without that cost:\n1. Reuse small blocks the program frees. A thread-local list per size serves the next allocation. Every collection drops the lists at its start. While a list is not empty, the region limit is set equal to the bump pointer, which sends the allocation to the slow path and leaves the fast path unchanged.\n2. Pace the floor by the measured cost of a collection and the allocation rate, so that collection time stays near 5% of the run. This also belongs to 3bbb229.\n\nAlso tried this round and dropped: a write prefetch 4 lines ahead of the small-object bump. No change on any row.\n\nRecommendation. Immix is at parity on time and equal or lower on memory, so it can stay an opt-in provider. It must not become the default before it handles allocation from several threads. Today a second allocating thread turns collection off.","files":null}]}